<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wasashatta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wasashatta was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanigalbat">Hanigalbat</a>, the rump of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> state, in the thirteenth century BCE. The Mitanni Empire profile records that rebellions led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shattuara-i">Shattuara I</a> and Wasashatta against Assyrian domination were suppressed by the Assyrian kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adad-nirari-i">Adad-nirari I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-i">Shalmaneser I</a>. These failures culminated in the full annexation of the kingdom by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> around 1250 BCE.</p></div>
